course: dictionary
lesson: 5285
title: Jumble: a mix in no order
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A jumble is an untidy mix of things that are not in any order. Your bedroom floor can be a jumble of toys, shoes and socks. Jumble is also a verb: if you jumble things, you mix them up so they are out of order.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The two friends tease him by saying his Mother's advice back to him all jumbled up, until his head spins.» Jumbled up means the words are mixed up and out of order, which is why his head spins.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "Saying his Mother's advice back to him all mixed up and out of order" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Jumble has a few other meanings too. In the UK, a jumble sale sells old things cheaply to raise money for a school or church. A word jumble is a puzzle where the letters are mixed up, and you put them back in order to find the word.
fact: Jumble can be a noun (a jumble of things) or a verb (to jumble things up).
fact: «Jumbled» means mixed up and out of order.
fact: A jumble sale is a sale of old things, sold cheaply in the UK to raise money.
fact: A word jumble is a puzzle with the letters mixed up.
fact: Useful phrases: a jumble of, jumbled up, jumble sale.
exercise: The bedroom floor was a jumble of toys, shoes and socks. What does jumble mean here? | *An untidy mix of things in no order | A loud crash | A neat row of shoes | A box for keeping toys
exercise: «The two friends tease him by saying his Mother's advice back to him all jumbled up.» What does jumbled up mean? | Lost for ever | Folded neatly | Read aloud slowly | *Mixed up and out of order
exercise: In the UK, what is a jumble sale for? | Winning a prize for the fastest runner | Giving out free sweets to children | *Selling old things cheaply to raise money | Teaching people to read
test: Which one is a word puzzle with the letters mixed up? | *A word jumble | A map of the town | A bus timetable | A jumble sale
test: What does "Please don't jumble my cards" ask you to do? | Count them carefully | Give them away to a friend | Keep them in order | *Mix them up so they are out of order
exam: «Stroking a paper clip with a magnet lines up its tiny magnets; dropping it jumbles them again.» What does jumbles them again mean? | Lines them up in neat rows | Paints them red | *Mixes them up out of order again | Makes them bigger
